# Sources used:
# - Shazam, Tolly Boy's YMW listings (opened 2026-10-20): Get on Bad (feat. Ciio & King Kembe), released December 30, 2018, label 1087489 Records DK2, 174 BPM, songwriter Youry Fleming; Oú Paté Vwey, released February 14, 2019, label YMW, 162 BPM, songwriter Fleming xavier Youry; GoDownGoDown, released January 19, 2020, label YMW, 169 BPM, songwriter Fleming Youry.
# - Shazam, Bay Li by YMW & Bilix (opened 2026-10-20): released July 14, 2020, label YMW X BILIX, 157 BPM, songwriters YMW and Franck Offranc, producers DWAYNE SKERRIT and Anne Arrindell; the page music video header reads "TOLLY BOYS & BILIX - BAY LI". Cited as a circle release, not as a Tolly Boy's YMW artist credit.
# - Shazam, Wizito listings (opened via search results, 2026-10-20): Payé (feat. Youry Ymw), released February 8, 2023, by YMW Tolly Boys; Love Me, released February 14, 2024, by YMW TOLLY BOYS, songwriter Bernard Gumbs, producer Sylvio Benjamin; TunTun (feat. Ti Al & Dj Chimik), released August 1, 2025, label YMW TOLLY BOYS, songwriters Ti Al and Bernard Gumbs. Label activity only; the full Wizito record is on this site Bernard Gumbs page.
# - Academic study, "An educated Sint Maartener? National belonging in a primary school on Sint Maarten", Globalisation, Societies and Education (ResearchGate record 335637940, consulted 2026-10-20): the Tolly Boys are described as local performers of bouyon music on Sint Maarten, and pupils in the studied primary school spontaneously sang their songs, including what the study calls their most famous song, quoted as "Tolly she want, tolly she go and get", the study glossing the word tolly as local slang for penis.
# Note: Tolly Boys, with an o, the Sint Maarten circle act and its label YMW Tolly Boys, are NOT Tallyboy, with an a, the Saint Lucia solo artist who has his own page on this site. No verified official social or streaming artist URL was opened for Tolly Boy's YMW itself, so sameAs is empty.

